  "general_notes": "This drawing contains some composite-style GD&T FCF, that is 2 FCFs (belonging to two different balloons) sharing the same GD&T symbol (in this drawing you'll see some profile symbols ⌓ and positional symbol ⌖ being of composite type. A compostie style GD&T FCF is two FCf written above and below one another, with the GD&T symbol preceding it covering both FCF (on the drawing, you might only be able to see one symbol, but because it's written on both FCF, it's considered that symbol independently. An example in this drawing is balloon 5 & 6, 20 & 21, 24 & 25, 26 & 27. This drawing also introduces a new GD&T symbol called Statistical Tolerance, written as ST enclosed in a hexagon, and for some reason when copied and pasted it becomes a ✞. You'll see it as  one of the added characteristics in rev B drawing.",
